-- Residential Tenancies Amendment (Rent Cap) Bill 2026 (WA), Bill No. 70,
-- as introduced in the Legislative Council on 7 May 2026 -- clauses 5 to
-- 9 and proposed ss.106-107. Encoded as the Residential Tenancies Act
-- 1987 would read if the Bill were enacted unamended.
--
-- NOT LAW. See the header of rent-cap-bill-rent.l4 for sources. The
-- unamended provisions are encoded in ../part-v-termination-notices.l4
-- and ../part-v-division-4-court-orders.l4; this module does not change
-- them. Findings are numbered B-nn and forks F-n (LQA/INCIDENTS.md).

§ `Clause 5 - Section 60(1) amended`

-- Amended s.60(1)(a)(ii): "a competent court terminates the agreement
-- under section 71 or 71BA". Amended s.60(1)(b): "lessor or" deleted, so
-- only the tenant's s.70A notice ends a fixed term under limb (b).

DECLARE `amended section 60 circumstances` HAS
    `the lessor or tenant gives notice of termination under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant delivers up vacant possession on or after the expiration of the period of notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a competent court terminates the agreement under section 71 or 71BA` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenancy is for a fixed term` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant gives a notice of termination under section 70A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor gives a notice of termination under section 70A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant delivers up possession on or after the day the term expires under section 70A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a competent court on the lessor's application terminates the agreement under section 72` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN c IS A `amended section 60 circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `amended section 60(1)(a) applies` IF
        c's `the lessor or tenant gives notice of termination under this Act`
    AND (
            c's `the tenant delivers up vacant possession on or after the expiration of the period of notice`
        OR  c's `a competent court terminates the agreement under section 71 or 71BA`
        )

@ref Residential Tenancies Amendment (Rent Cap) Bill 2026 (WA) cl.5, amended s.60(1)(b)
@export Decide whether amended s.60(1)(b) terminates a fixed-term agreement at the end of its term
GIVEN c IS A `amended section 60 circumstances` @desc Fixed-term end facts. After the Bill only a tenant's s.70A notice counts; a lessor's notice under s.70A no longer exists. The agreement ends when the tenant delivers up possession on or after the day the term expires, or when a court terminates it under s.72 on the lessor's application.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `amended section 60(1)(b) applies` IF
        c's `the tenancy is for a fixed term`
    AND c's `the tenant gives a notice of termination under section 70A`
    AND (
            c's `the tenant delivers up possession on or after the day the term expires under section 70A`
        OR  c's `a competent court on the lessor's application terminates the agreement under section 72`
        )

§§ `Clause 5 -- illustrations`

`lessor's end-of-term notice, tenant stays` MEANS `amended section 60 circumstances` WITH
    `the lessor or tenant gives notice of termination under this Act` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant delivers up vacant possession on or after the expiration of the period of notice` IS FALSE,
    `a competent court terminates the agreement under section 71 or 71BA` IS FALSE,
    `the tenancy is for a fixed term` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant gives a notice of termination under section 70A` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor gives a notice of termination under section 70A` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant delivers up possession on or after the day the term expires under section 70A` IS FALSE,
    `a competent court on the lessor's application terminates the agreement under section 72` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `amended section 60(1)(b) applies` `lessor's end-of-term notice, tenant stays` EQUALS FALSE

§ `Clause 6 - Section 64 amended`

DECLARE `section 64 ground` IS ONE OF
    `the lessor genuinely intends to live in the premises`
    `the lessor genuinely intends that the lessor's immediate relative live in the premises`
    `the lessor genuinely intends that another person with a close family or personal relationship with the lessor live in the premises`
    `the lessor genuinely intends to sell the premises`
    `the lessor genuinely intends to reconstruct, renovate or make major repairs that cannot reasonably be carried out with the tenant living in the premises`
    `the lessor genuinely intends to use the premises for another lawful use other than as residential premises`

DECLARE `amended section 64 notice` HAS
    `the notice is in the form required by section 61` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement creates a periodic tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ground stated` IS A `section 64 ground`
    `the lessor genuinely holds the intention stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is accompanied by written evidence supporting the ground` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of notice before vacant possession is required` IS A NUMBER
    `proceedings are pending for an order or an order is in force under section 32` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proceedings are pending under section 31AB or an order under section 31AB(5) is in force` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s.64(2A): 3 months for ground (e), 6 months for ground (f), 60 days
-- otherwise. Months are calendar months; the figures below are the
-- SHORTEST day-counts those can be (3 months from 1 February in a
-- common year is 89 days; 6 months from 1 September is 181 days). A
-- notice of 89-92 or 181-184 days must be checked against the calendar.

GIVEN g IS A `section 64 ground`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the shortest period of notice for the ground in days` IS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `the lessor genuinely intends to reconstruct, renovate or make major repairs that cannot reasonably be carried out with the tenant living in the premises` THEN 89
    WHEN `the lessor genuinely intends to use the premises for another lawful use other than as residential premises` THEN 181
    OTHERWISE 60

-- s.65(1)(a), unamended: a s.64 notice is ineffectual while s.32
-- proceedings are pending or an s.32 order is in force. The Bill does not
-- extend s.65 to s.31AB (B-10).

GIVEN n IS A `amended section 64 notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 65(1)(a) makes the notice ineffectual` IF
    n's `proceedings are pending for an order or an order is in force under section 32`

@ref Residential Tenancies Amendment (Rent Cap) Bill 2026 (WA) cl.6, amended s.64(1)-(2A) and (5); s.65(1)(a)
@export Decide whether a lessor's notice terminating a periodic tenancy on a ground in amended s.64 is effectual
GIVEN n IS A `amended section 64 notice` @desc A lessor's notice under amended s.64. Only for a periodic tenancy that is not a social housing tenancy. The lessor must genuinely hold the intention stated, the notice must be accompanied by written evidence supporting it, and the period of notice must be at least 60 days, 3 months (renovation or major repairs) or 6 months (another lawful use). Ineffectual while s.32 proceedings are pending or an s.32 order is in force.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor's notice on a section 64 ground is effectual` IF
        n's `the notice is in the form required by section 61`
    AND n's `the agreement creates a periodic tenancy`
    AND NOT n's `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement`
    AND n's `the lessor genuinely holds the intention stated`
    AND n's `the notice is accompanied by written evidence supporting the ground`
    AND n's `days of notice before vacant possession is required` AT LEAST `the shortest period of notice for the ground in days` (n's `the ground stated`)
    AND NOT `section 65(1)(a) makes the notice ineffectual` n

§§ `Section 64(4)(c) unamended -- earliest possession day`

-- s.64(3)-(4) are not amended. On the tenant's application to extend,
-- the court may instead order possession from "the later of" (i) a day
-- not less than 60 days after the notice was received, or (ii) a day
-- within 7 days after the order. The earliest day it can choose is the
-- later of day 60 and the day after the order. Days count from receipt.
-- Proposed s.71BA(4)(c) repeats the formula (B-05).

GIVEN `days after the notice was received that the order is made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the earliest possession day a court may order under the 60-day formula` IS
    IF `days after the notice was received that the order is made` PLUS 1 GREATER THAN 60
    THEN `days after the notice was received that the order is made` PLUS 1
    ELSE 60

GIVEN g IS A `section 64 ground`, `days after the notice was received that the order is made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a court may order possession before the section 64(2A) notice period for the ground has run` IF
    `the earliest possession day a court may order under the 60-day formula` `days after the notice was received that the order is made`
        LESS THAN `the shortest period of notice for the ground in days` g

§§ `Clause 6 -- illustrations`

`renovation notice, 3 months, with evidence` MEANS `amended section 64 notice` WITH
    `the notice is in the form required by section 61` IS TRUE,
    `the agreement creates a periodic tenancy` IS TRUE,
    `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the ground stated` IS `the lessor genuinely intends to reconstruct, renovate or make major repairs that cannot reasonably be carried out with the tenant living in the premises`,
    `the lessor genuinely holds the intention stated` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is accompanied by written evidence supporting the ground` IS TRUE,
    `days of notice before vacant possession is required` IS 92,
    `proceedings are pending for an order or an order is in force under section 32` IS FALSE,
    `proceedings are pending under section 31AB or an order under section 31AB(5) is in force` IS FALSE

`renovation notice, 60 days` MEANS `amended section 64 notice` WITH
    `the notice is in the form required by section 61` IS TRUE,
    `the agreement creates a periodic tenancy` IS TRUE,
    `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the ground stated` IS `the lessor genuinely intends to reconstruct, renovate or make major repairs that cannot reasonably be carried out with the tenant living in the premises`,
    `the lessor genuinely holds the intention stated` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is accompanied by written evidence supporting the ground` IS TRUE,
    `days of notice before vacant possession is required` IS 60,
    `proceedings are pending for an order or an order is in force under section 32` IS FALSE,
    `proceedings are pending under section 31AB or an order under section 31AB(5) is in force` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the lessor's notice on a section 64 ground is effectual` `renovation notice, 3 months, with evidence` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the lessor's notice on a section 64 ground is effectual` `renovation notice, 60 days` EQUALS FALSE

-- B-05: the tenant applies within 7 days to extend a 6-month "other
-- lawful use" notice; the court hears it on day 20 and, under unamended
-- s.64(4)(c), may order possession from day 60 -- four months before the
-- notice the lessor was required to give would have run.

#ASSERT `the earliest possession day a court may order under the 60-day formula` 20 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `a court may order possession before the section 64(2A) notice period for the ground has run` `the lessor genuinely intends to use the premises for another lawful use other than as residential premises` 20 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a court may order possession before the section 64(2A) notice period for the ground has run` `the lessor genuinely intends to reconstruct, renovate or make major repairs that cannot reasonably be carried out with the tenant living in the premises` 20 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a court may order possession before the section 64(2A) notice period for the ground has run` `the lessor genuinely intends to sell the premises` 20 EQUALS FALSE

-- B-10: the lessor's s.31AB application to lift the rent above the cap
-- is refused and a 1-year s.31AB(5) order is made. A "sell" notice given
-- the next week is not caught by s.65(1)(a), which reaches s.32 only.

`sale notice while a section 31AB order is in force` MEANS `amended section 64 notice` WITH
    `the notice is in the form required by section 61` IS TRUE,
    `the agreement creates a periodic tenancy` IS TRUE,
    `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the ground stated` IS `the lessor genuinely intends to sell the premises`,
    `the lessor genuinely holds the intention stated` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is accompanied by written evidence supporting the ground` IS TRUE,
    `days of notice before vacant possession is required` IS 60,
    `proceedings are pending for an order or an order is in force under section 32` IS FALSE,
    `proceedings are pending under section 31AB or an order under section 31AB(5) is in force` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the lessor's notice on a section 64 ground is effectual` `sale notice while a section 31AB order is in force` EQUALS TRUE

§ `Clause 7 - Section 70A amended`

-- Amended s.70A(2): "the term of a residential tenancy agreement (other
-- than a social housing tenancy agreement) does not end on the expiry
-- day unless the tenant gives a notice of termination". s.70A(3)-(5)
-- are kept: the notice at least 30 days before the possession day, and
-- the possession day not earlier than the expiry day.

DECLARE `amended end of fixed term facts` HAS
    `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has given a notice of termination specifying a possession day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days before the possession day that the tenant's notice was given` IS A NUMBER
    `the possession day relative to the expiry day` IS A NUMBER
    `the lessor has given a notice of termination specifying a possession day` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN f IS A `amended end of fixed term facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `amended section 70A(2) applies to the agreement` IF
    NOT f's `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement`

GIVEN f IS A `amended end of fixed term facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant has given a notice under amended section 70A` IF
        `amended section 70A(2) applies to the agreement` f
    AND f's `the tenant has given a notice of termination specifying a possession day`
    AND f's `days before the possession day that the tenant's notice was given` AT LEAST 30
    AND f's `the possession day relative to the expiry day` AT LEAST 0

@ref Residential Tenancies Amendment (Rent Cap) Bill 2026 (WA) cl.7, amended s.70A(2)
@export Decide whether, after the Bill, amended s.70A(2) stops the fixed term ending on the expiry day
GIVEN f IS A `amended end of fixed term facts` @desc Fixed-term end facts. Offsets are days relative to the expiry day. Amended s.70A(2) does not apply to a social housing tenancy agreement. For other agreements the term does not end on the expiry day unless the tenant gives a notice at least 30 days before a possession day that is not before the expiry day. A lessor's notice has no effect.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `amended section 70A(2) stops the term ending on the expiry day` IF
        `amended section 70A(2) applies to the agreement` f
    AND NOT `the tenant has given a notice under amended section 70A` f

-- Fork F-2: when s.70A(2) stops the term ending, does the agreement stay
-- a fixed-term tenancy (the words of s.70A(2)) or continue as a periodic
-- tenancy (s.76C(2))? Amended s.64 reaches only a periodic tenancy, and
-- s.63(4) excludes a fixed term during its currency, so the answer
-- decides whether the lessor has any ground-based route at all.

GIVEN f IS A `amended end of fixed term facts`, `reading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `after the expiry day the lessor can give a notice under amended section 64` IF
        `amended section 70A(2) stops the term ending on the expiry day` f
    AND `reading`

§§ `Clause 7 -- illustrations`

`private fixed term, lessor gives end-of-term notice` MEANS `amended end of fixed term facts` WITH
    `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant has given a notice of termination specifying a possession day` IS FALSE,
    `days before the possession day that the tenant's notice was given` IS 0,
    `the possession day relative to the expiry day` IS 0,
    `the lessor has given a notice of termination specifying a possession day` IS TRUE

-- B-07: social housing. Amended s.70A(2) no longer applies, so nothing
-- in s.70A stops a social housing fixed term ending on its expiry day,
-- and the social housing tenant's end-of-term notice has gone: the
-- tenant's notice is not "a notice referred to in subsection (2)".

`social housing fixed term, tenant gives end-of-term notice` MEANS `amended end of fixed term facts` WITH
    `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant has given a notice of termination specifying a possession day` IS TRUE,
    `days before the possession day that the tenant's notice was given` IS 30,
    `the possession day relative to the expiry day` IS 0,
    `the lessor has given a notice of termination specifying a possession day` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `amended section 70A(2) stops the term ending on the expiry day` `private fixed term, lessor gives end-of-term notice` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the tenant has given a notice under amended section 70A` `social housing fixed term, tenant gives end-of-term notice` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `amended section 70A(2) stops the term ending on the expiry day` `social housing fixed term, tenant gives end-of-term notice` EQUALS FALSE

-- F-2, the two readings: TRUE = s.76C (periodic), FALSE = fixed term
-- continues.

#ASSERT `after the expiry day the lessor can give a notice under amended section 64` `private fixed term, lessor gives end-of-term notice` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `after the expiry day the lessor can give a notice under amended section 64` `private fixed term, lessor gives end-of-term notice` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Clause 8 - Proposed section 71BA`

DECLARE `section 71BA ground` IS ONE OF
    `the lessor genuinely intends to sell the social housing premises`
    `the lessor genuinely intends to reconstruct, renovate or make major repairs that cannot reasonably be carried out with the tenant living in the social housing premises`
    `the lessor genuinely intends to use the premises for another lawful use other than as social housing premises`

DECLARE `section 71BA notice` HAS
    `the notice is in the form required by section 61` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ground stated` IS A `section 71BA ground`
    `the lessor genuinely holds the intention stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of notice before vacant possession is required` IS A NUMBER
    `the tenancy is for a fixed term during its currency` IS A BOOLEAN

-- B-08: s.71BA, unlike s.63(4), unamended s.64(5) and s.71J(5), says
-- nothing about a fixed term during its currency. Encoded as written:
-- the fixed-term field is read by nothing.

@ref Residential Tenancies Amendment (Rent Cap) Bill 2026 (WA) cl.8, proposed s.71BA(1)-(2)
@export Decide whether a social housing lessor's notice of termination under proposed s.71BA is effectual
GIVEN n IS A `section 71BA notice` @desc A social housing lessor's notice on the ground that it genuinely intends to sell, to reconstruct, renovate or make major repairs that cannot be done with the tenant in residence, or to use the premises other than as social housing. The period of notice must be at least 90 days. The Bill does not say whether a fixed term during its currency can be ended this way; the encoding follows the words and does not exclude it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor's notice under section 71BA is effectual` IF
        n's `the notice is in the form required by section 61`
    AND n's `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement`
    AND n's `the lessor genuinely holds the intention stated`
    AND n's `days of notice before vacant possession is required` AT LEAST 90

§§ `Clause 8 -- illustrations`

`social housing sale, mid fixed term` MEANS `section 71BA notice` WITH
    `the notice is in the form required by section 61` IS TRUE,
    `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the ground stated` IS `the lessor genuinely intends to sell the social housing premises`,
    `the lessor genuinely holds the intention stated` IS TRUE,
    `days of notice before vacant possession is required` IS 90,
    `the tenancy is for a fixed term during its currency` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the lessor's notice under section 71BA is effectual` `social housing sale, mid fixed term` EQUALS TRUE

-- B-05 (s.71BA limb): 90 days' notice, but on the tenant's own
-- application to extend, s.71BA(4)(c) lets the court order possession
-- from day 60.

#ASSERT (`the earliest possession day a court may order under the 60-day formula` 10) LESS THAN 90

§ `Clause 9 - Section 72 amended`

-- Amended s.72(1): "Where a tenant under an agreement gives notice of
-- termination under section 70A and the tenant fails to deliver up
-- possession ... the lessor may ... apply". The application is still the
-- lessor's -- as it always was. That matters for proposed s.107 (B-09).

§ `Clause 10 - Proposed sections 106 and 107`

DECLARE `lessor notice in effect immediately before commencement day` HAS
    `the notice was given under previous section 64(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice was given under previous section 70A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant is in possession of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has applied under section 64(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has applied under section 71 or 72 for termination and possession` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Previous s.72(1): "the lessor may ... apply". No provision lets a
-- tenant apply under s.72(1), so the condition in proposed s.107(2)(b)
-- and (4)(b) -- "an application by the tenant under previous section
-- 72(1)" -- is fixed.

`previous section 72(1) permits an application by the tenant` MEANS FALSE

GIVEN x IS A `lessor notice in effect immediately before commencement day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 106 applies` IF
        x's `the notice was given under previous section 64(1)`
    AND x's `the notice is in effect`
    AND x's `the tenant is in possession of the premises`

GIVEN x IS A `lessor notice in effect immediately before commencement day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 107 applies` IF
        x's `the notice was given under previous section 70A(2)`
    AND x's `the notice is in effect`
    AND x's `the tenant is in possession of the premises`

@ref Residential Tenancies Amendment (Rent Cap) Bill 2026 (WA) cl.10, proposed ss.106(2), 106(4)(a), 107(3), 107(5)(a)
@export Decide whether a lessor's pre-commencement notice under previous s.64(1) or s.70A(2) becomes ineffectual on commencement day
GIVEN x IS A `lessor notice in effect immediately before commencement day` @desc A lessor's notice in effect immediately before commencement day while the tenant is in possession: either a no-grounds notice under previous s.64(1) or an end-of-fixed-term notice under previous s.70A(2). Either becomes ineffectual on commencement day, whatever applications are pending.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is ineffectual on commencement day` IF
        `section 106 applies` x
    OR  `section 107 applies` x

GIVEN x IS A `lessor notice in effect immediately before commencement day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a pending application is taken to be dismissed` IF
        (   `section 106 applies` x
        AND x's `the tenant has applied under section 64(3)`
        )
    OR  (   `section 107 applies` x
        AND `previous section 72(1) permits an application by the tenant`
        )

§§ `Clause 10 -- illustrations`

-- B-09: a fixed term expired; the lessor's previous-s.70A notice named
-- the expiry day; the tenant held over and the lessor applied under
-- s.72 before commencement. On commencement the notice is ineffectual,
-- but the lessor's application is not dismissed: s.107(5)(b) dismisses
-- only a tenant's s.72(1) application, which cannot exist.

`lessor's section 72 application pending` MEANS `lessor notice in effect immediately before commencement day` WITH
    `the notice was given under previous section 64(1)` IS FALSE,
    `the notice was given under previous section 70A(2)` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is in effect` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant is in possession of the premises` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant has applied under section 64(3)` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has applied under section 71 or 72 for termination and possession` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the notice is ineffectual on commencement day` `lessor's section 72 application pending` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a pending application is taken to be dismissed` `lessor's section 72 application pending` EQUALS FALSE

-- B-09 (s.106 limb): the same gap for a lessor's s.71 application on a
-- previous-s.64 notice. The tenant's s.64(3) application is dismissed;
-- the lessor's is not mentioned.

`lessor's section 71 application pending` MEANS `lessor notice in effect immediately before commencement day` WITH
    `the notice was given under previous section 64(1)` IS TRUE,
    `the notice was given under previous section 70A(2)` IS FALSE,
    `the notice is in effect` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant is in possession of the premises` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant has applied under section 64(3)` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has applied under section 71 or 72 for termination and possession` IS TRUE

`tenant's section 64(3) application pending` MEANS `lessor notice in effect immediately before commencement day` WITH
    `the notice was given under previous section 64(1)` IS TRUE,
    `the notice was given under previous section 70A(2)` IS FALSE,
    `the notice is in effect` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant is in possession of the premises` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant has applied under section 64(3)` IS TRUE,
    `the lessor has applied under section 71 or 72 for termination and possession` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the notice is ineffectual on commencement day` `lessor's section 71 application pending` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a pending application is taken to be dismissed` `lessor's section 71 application pending` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `a pending application is taken to be dismissed` `tenant's section 64(3) application pending` EQUALS TRUE
